==English==

===Etymology===
From a modern frequentative form of {{m|en|draw}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|draw|le}}. Compare {{m|en|draggle}}. Compare also {{cog|nl|dralen||to drag out, delay, linger, tarry, dawdle}}, Old Danish {{m|da|dravle||to linger, loiter}}, {{cog|is|dralla||to loiter, linger}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɹɔːl/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-drawl.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɹɔl/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɹɑl/|a=cot-caught}}
* {{rfv-pron|en}} {{IPA|en|/d͡ʒɹɑːw/|a=US,paragon}}
: {{rhymes|en|ɔːl|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[drag]] on slowly and heavily; to [[while]] or [[dawdle]] away time indolently.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[utter]] or pronounce in a dull, spiritless tone, as if by dragging out the utterance.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[move]] slowly and heavily; move in a dull, slow, lazy manner.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Thomas Dekker|page=3-4|chapter=|title=The guls horne-booke|url=https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/eebo/A20060.0001.001/1:5?rgn=div1;subview=detail;type=simple;view=fulltext;q1=drawling|year=1609|volume=|passage=Tush, tush, ''Tarleton'', ''Kemp'', nor ''Singer'', nor all the litter of Fooles that now come '''drawling''' behinde them, neuer plaid the Clownes more naturally then the arrantest Sot of you all, shall, if hee will but boyle my Instructions in his brainepan.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Fernando de Rojas|page=36|chapter=|title=The Spanish bavvd, represented in Celestina [...]|url=https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/eebo/A18331.0001.001/1:6?rgn=div1;subview=detail;type=simple;view=fulltext;q1=drawling|year=1631|volume=|passage=Looke what leysure the old bearded Bawd takes / How softly she goes / How one leg comes '''drawling''' after another / Now she has her money, her armes are broken.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[speak]] with a slow, spiritless utterance, from [[affectation]], laziness, or lack of interest.
#* {{RQ:Landor Imaginary Conversations|3|Lord Brooke and Sir Philip Sidney|passage=talk sometimes a pestilence , and sometimes a hero , mostly in a '''drawling''' and dreaming way about it}}

